| Name         | Description                         | Units  |   Default value |
| ------------ | ----------------------------------- | ------ | --------------- |
| `r_foot`         | Foot position relative to the centre of mass, body frame (FRD)                         | m  |   [0.12, 0.12, 0.1] |
| `z_ground`         | Ground height in NED (down positive)                         | m  |   0.0 |
| `k`         | Contact stiffness                         | N/m  |   600.0 |
| `c`         | Contact damping per unit penetration (Hunt-Crossley)                         | N.s/m2  |   4000.0 |
| `mu`         | Coulomb friction coefficient                         | --  |   0.6 |
| `v_slip`         | Slip velocity at which friction reaches about 70% of mu * F_n                         | m/s  |   0.01 |
| `delta_s`         | Smoothing length of the penetration positive part                         | m  |   1e-4 |
| `s_eps`         | Smoothing of the max(., 0) on the normal stiffness term                         | N/m  |   1.0 |

## Connectors

 * `port` - Body-fixed mechanical port of a rigid airframe.

Conventions (ArduPilot): world frame is NED (north, east, down), body frame is
FRD (forward, right, down). The airframe owns the potentials; every other
component reads them and returns the force/torque it needs through the flows.

Flow sign convention (same as Frame3D): `f` and `tau` are the force and the
torque exerted ON the component THROUGH the port, resolved in the body frame,
torque taken about the airframe centre of mass. A massless element that applies
an external force F at body point r therefore sets f = -F and tau = -(r x F). ([`BodyPort`](@ref))

